        "titulo": "Days of the week: «в» + day",
        "explicacao": "In Russian, the days of the week are written with a small letter, unlike English, where Monday, Tuesday and the rest always get a capital. To say \"on Monday\", use «в» + the day: «в понедельник». Days that end in -а change it to -у (the accusative): «в пятницу», «в субботу», «в среду». Before «вторник» you use «во»: «во вторник». «Воскресенье» does not change: «в воскресенье».",
        "comparacao": "in English we say \"on Monday\" or \"on Mondays\". In Russian the day takes only «в» and the accusative ending, and there is no capital letter.",
